# convert metaphaln abundance to gtdbdk named abundance file using metaphlan script
# now at species level we need to either build metabolic models or match it to already built metabolic models (the built metabolic models are part of the micom db which we will use)
#the following script is @species level
#uhgg gapseq is chosen given that these are gut fecal sample (agora2 could/should be checked to see if nomenclature resulting in a mapping issue)
#given that its gtdbdk that we have employed we have chosen  uhgg gtdbdk species mapping file from zenodo (427mb)
